1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,686
Bombay.

2
00:00:00,925 --> 00:00:02,028
Nineteen twenty four.

3
00:00:02,419 --> 00:00:05,686
A man walks into a bank, carrying his wife's diamond.

4
00:00:06,017 --> 00:00:08,393
Two hundred and forty five carats.

5
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:12,098
More than twice the size of the Kohinoor, as it is today.

6
00:00:12,736 --> 00:00:14,045
He isn't here to sell it.

7
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:17,148
He wants a loan, with the diamond as the guarantee.

8
00:00:17,661 --> 00:00:18,992
Why would a man do that?

9
00:00:19,408 --> 00:00:27,283
Because more than fourteen hundred kilometres away, in a steel town cut out of the jungle, thousands of workers are waiting for their wages.

10
00:00:27,547 --> 00:00:30,862
And the company that pays them is almost out of money.

11
00:00:31,474 --> 00:00:33,083
You may never have heard his name.

12
00:00:33,355 --> 00:00:34,851
Sir Dorabji Tata.

13
00:00:35,194 --> 00:00:37,150
The company is Tata Steel.

14
00:00:37,568 --> 00:00:38,898
Now look around you today.

15
00:00:39,214 --> 00:00:40,585
The salt in your kitchen.

16
00:00:40,603 --> 00:00:41,840
The tea in your cup.

17
00:00:41,965 --> 00:00:43,392
The steel in our bridges.

18
00:00:43,488 --> 00:00:44,950
The plane over your head.

19
00:00:45,603 --> 00:00:46,067
Tata.

20
00:00:46,624 --> 00:00:51,117
And yet you won't find a single Tata at the top of any rich list.

21
00:00:51,408 --> 00:00:52,533
How is that possible?

22
00:00:52,836 --> 00:00:54,706
The answer is in this bank.

23
00:00:54,859 --> 00:00:56,947
In what happens to that diamond.

24
00:00:57,228 --> 00:01:03,064
Because a choice this man makes, eight years later, still decides who controls Tata today.

25
00:01:03,429 --> 00:01:07,275
And in twenty twenty six, that choice has turned into a fight.

26
00:01:07,592 --> 00:01:09,687
By the end of this film, you'll see how.

27
00:01:10,007 --> 00:01:13,791
But why would a man pawn his wife's diamond for a steel plant?

28
00:01:14,062 --> 00:01:17,401
To understand that, we go back to the man who dreamed it.

29
00:01:18,753 --> 00:01:20,252
Eighteen sixty eight.

30
00:01:20,726 --> 00:01:25,667
Bombay is a city of ships and cotton, and most of the money flows one way.

31
00:01:26,058 --> 00:01:26,569
Out.

32
00:01:27,041 --> 00:01:29,548
Indian cotton sails to the mills of England.

33
00:01:29,767 --> 00:01:32,456
The cloth comes back, and Indians pay for it.

34
00:01:32,809 --> 00:01:39,448
That year, a twenty nine year old Parsi from Navsari starts a trading firm with twenty one thousand rupees.

35
00:01:39,794 --> 00:01:42,093
His name is Jamsetji Tata.

36
00:01:42,482 --> 00:01:48,708
Like many traders of his time, his family's business ran on cotton and on opium, sold to China.

37
00:01:49,052 --> 00:01:52,355
That is part of this story too, and it's worth saying out loud.

38
00:01:52,707 --> 00:01:55,445
But Jamsetji keeps asking one question.

39
00:01:55,862 --> 00:01:59,746
Why send our cotton away, when we can spin it right here?

40
00:02:00,013 --> 00:02:00,991
So what does he do?

41
00:02:01,361 --> 00:02:02,558
He builds a mill.

42
00:02:02,791 --> 00:02:05,002
Not in Bombay, where everyone builds.

43
00:02:05,202 --> 00:02:07,880
In Nagpur, right where the cotton grows.

44
00:02:08,085 --> 00:02:11,485
It opens on the first of January, eighteen seventy seven.

45
00:02:11,678 --> 00:02:15,526
The same day Queen Victoria is proclaimed Empress of India.

46
00:02:15,773 --> 00:02:17,945
So he names it Empress Mills.

47
00:02:18,148 --> 00:02:20,518
Then he does something strange for his time.

48
00:02:20,825 --> 00:02:23,256
He starts a pension fund for his workers.

49
00:02:23,525 --> 00:02:26,377
Later, he pays them when they're hurt on the job.

50
00:02:26,598 --> 00:02:27,906
Was it pure kindness?

51
00:02:28,174 --> 00:02:30,882
He answered that himself, in eighteen ninety five.

52
00:02:31,149 --> 00:02:34,012
He was no kinder than anyone else, he said.

53
00:02:34,266 --> 00:02:37,972
But healthy workers were the sure foundation of his success.

54
00:02:38,286 --> 00:02:41,392
Now, you've probably heard the most famous Tata story.

55
00:02:41,601 --> 00:02:45,216
Jamsetji is turned away from a whites only hotel in Bombay.

56
00:02:45,419 --> 00:02:48,412
So he builds the Taj, to answer the insult.

57
00:02:48,647 --> 00:02:50,535
It's a great story, isn't it?

58
00:02:50,784 --> 00:02:54,436
But historians have found no record that it ever happened.

59
00:02:54,937 --> 00:02:57,495
What is on record is the hotel itself.

60
00:02:57,891 --> 00:03:01,659
It opens in December, nineteen oh three, on the Bombay waterfront.

61
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:03,812
Designed by an Indian architect.

62
00:03:03,986 --> 00:03:05,613
Lit by electricity.

63
00:03:06,076 --> 00:03:07,272
Hold on to this hotel.

64
00:03:08,195 --> 00:03:11,512
It comes back in this story, on the worst night of its life.

65
00:03:12,210 --> 00:03:14,640
But a hotel was never his biggest dream.

66
00:03:14,864 --> 00:03:17,049
Jamsetji had three bigger ones.

67
00:03:17,287 --> 00:03:20,992
A steel plant, so India could make its own rails and bridges.

68
00:03:21,303 --> 00:03:24,120
Power from the monsoon rains of the Western Ghats.

69
00:03:24,330 --> 00:03:29,258
And a world class institute of science, so Indians could invent, not just buy.

70
00:03:29,663 --> 00:03:33,816
For the institute alone, he offers property worth thirty lakh rupees.

71
00:03:34,217 --> 00:03:36,324
The hardest of the three is steel.

72
00:03:36,622 --> 00:03:37,104
Why?

73
00:03:37,442 --> 00:03:43,412
Because to make steel, you need iron ore, the right coal and water, all in one place.

74
00:03:43,706 --> 00:03:46,858
And for years, every place he tries is wrong.

75
00:03:48,484 --> 00:03:51,291
One site has ore, but the coal is useless.

76
00:03:51,505 --> 00:03:53,567
Another has coal, but no water.

77
00:03:53,879 --> 00:03:58,277
Jamsetji even crosses the world to America, to find the right engineer.

78
00:03:58,588 --> 00:04:02,279
In a small, crowded office in New York, he finds his man.

79
00:04:02,543 --> 00:04:04,261
An American steel expert.

80
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:08,234
Then, in February nineteen oh four, a letter reaches him.

81
00:04:08,483 --> 00:04:12,072
It's from an Indian geologist, a man who studies rocks.

82
00:04:12,348 --> 00:04:13,790
Pramatha Nath Bose.

83
00:04:14,071 --> 00:04:17,419
He has been walking the hills of Mayurbhanj, in today's Odisha.

84
00:04:17,682 --> 00:04:19,514
And he has found iron ore.

85
00:04:19,768 --> 00:04:20,812
A lot of it.

86
00:04:21,045 --> 00:04:23,982
This is the letter that will build Tata Steel.

87
00:04:25,251 --> 00:04:30,316
But three months later, on a trip to Germany, Jamsetji Tata dies.

88
00:04:30,753 --> 00:04:32,300
He never sees those hills.

89
00:04:32,597 --> 00:04:33,736
No steel plant.

90
00:04:33,852 --> 00:04:35,050
No power company.

91
00:04:35,255 --> 00:04:36,295
No institute.

92
00:04:36,798 --> 00:04:38,657
So who carries the dream now?

93
00:04:38,988 --> 00:04:39,684
His son.

94
00:04:39,853 --> 00:04:40,636
Dorabji.

95
00:04:40,989 --> 00:04:43,417
And Dorabji does not run it from an office.

96
00:04:43,572 --> 00:04:48,020
He has already been out in the jungle himself, with the men searching for iron.

97
00:04:48,300 --> 00:04:51,520
Now they go back, looking for one perfect spot.

98
00:04:51,802 --> 00:04:56,529
They find it near a small village called Sakchi, right where two rivers meet.

99
00:04:56,841 --> 00:04:57,744
Ore nearby.

100
00:04:57,975 --> 00:04:58,856
Coal nearby.

101
00:04:59,056 --> 00:05:00,408
Water all year.

102
00:05:00,750 --> 00:05:02,166
Now they need money.

103
00:05:02,420 --> 00:05:03,639
A lot of money.

104
00:05:03,980 --> 00:05:05,327
Where do you even find it?

105
00:05:05,578 --> 00:05:07,000
They try London first.

106
00:05:07,175 --> 00:05:08,716
The answer is cold.

107
00:05:08,988 --> 00:05:12,477
So in nineteen oh seven, the Tatas take a huge risk.

108
00:05:12,869 --> 00:05:14,273
They ask India.

109
00:05:16,091 --> 00:05:18,013
Bombay, nineteen oh seven.

110
00:05:18,172 --> 00:05:19,671
The share office opens.

111
00:05:19,880 --> 00:05:21,037
And the people come.

112
00:05:21,368 --> 00:05:22,078
Who were they?

113
00:05:22,349 --> 00:05:24,452
One man who was there wrote it down.

114
00:05:24,671 --> 00:05:26,277
Old and young, he said.

115
00:05:26,445 --> 00:05:27,619
Rich and poor.

116
00:05:27,781 --> 00:05:28,976
Men and women.

117
00:05:29,201 --> 00:05:31,291
They came, offering their mites.

118
00:05:31,367 --> 00:05:32,336
Their mites.

119
00:05:32,438 --> 00:05:33,698
Their small savings.

120
00:05:33,842 --> 00:05:35,305
A little from each of them.

121
00:05:35,576 --> 00:05:40,418
In a matter of weeks, about eight thousand Indians put up the entire capital.

122
00:05:40,624 --> 00:05:42,900
Two crore thirty one lakh rupees.

123
00:05:43,216 --> 00:05:45,340
Now imagine you're standing in that line.

124
00:05:45,618 --> 00:05:47,375
India is ruled by Britain.

125
00:05:47,545 --> 00:05:51,412
And you're about to bet your savings that Indians can make steel.

126
00:05:51,801 --> 00:05:52,703
Would you have done it?

127
00:05:52,993 --> 00:05:54,811
Not everyone believed, of course.

128
00:05:54,982 --> 00:06:01,552
According to Tata's own histories, a senior British railway official, Sir Frederick Upcott, laughed at the idea.

129
00:06:01,888 --> 00:06:05,638
He said he would eat every pound of steel rail they managed to make.

130
00:06:05,953 --> 00:06:09,187
So how do you turn a hill of red rock into steel?

131
00:06:09,508 --> 00:06:11,660
You build a tower of fire.

132
00:06:12,163 --> 00:06:17,447
Iron ore, limestone, and coke, a kind of baked coal, go in at the top.

133
00:06:17,743 --> 00:06:19,742
Hot air blasts in at the bottom.

134
00:06:20,026 --> 00:06:22,958
And out comes iron, as a glowing liquid.

135
00:06:23,267 --> 00:06:25,124
Refine it, and you have steel.

136
00:06:25,582 --> 00:06:28,597
The first iron flows in December nineteen eleven.

137
00:06:28,808 --> 00:06:30,846
The first steel, in nineteen twelve.

138
00:06:31,338 --> 00:06:33,757
Two years later, the world goes to war.

139
00:06:34,127 --> 00:06:37,736
Britain's armies need rails, in the Middle East and in Africa.

140
00:06:37,996 --> 00:06:40,495
And many of those rails come from Tata.

141
00:06:40,968 --> 00:06:44,538
Tata's own records put it at about fifteen hundred miles.

142
00:06:44,884 --> 00:06:49,484
Years later, as the Tata story goes, Dorabji had a reply for Upcott.

143
00:06:49,765 --> 00:06:54,178
If he had kept his promise, he would have had some indigestion.

144
00:06:54,571 --> 00:06:57,245
In nineteen nineteen, the town gets a new name.

145
00:06:57,492 --> 00:06:58,371
Jamshedpur.

146
00:06:58,981 --> 00:07:00,959
After the man who never saw it.

147
00:07:01,222 --> 00:07:03,199
And his other dreams come true too.

148
00:07:03,428 --> 00:07:06,499
The institute opens in Bangalore in nineteen eleven.

149
00:07:06,724 --> 00:07:09,398
Today it's the Indian Institute of Science.

150
00:07:09,626 --> 00:07:15,071
And from nineteen fifteen, monsoon lakes in the Western Ghats send power to Bombay's mills.

151
00:07:15,289 --> 00:07:18,700
So the dreamer is gone, but every dream is alive.

152
00:07:19,180 --> 00:07:21,312
It should be a happy ending, shouldn't it?

153
00:07:22,532 --> 00:07:23,244
It isn't.

154
00:07:24,602 --> 00:07:26,822
A steel town is no fairy tale.

155
00:07:27,101 --> 00:07:30,126
In nineteen twenty two, the workers go on strike.

156
00:07:30,431 --> 00:07:32,061
Then the good years end.

157
00:07:32,315 --> 00:07:33,289
Prices fall.

158
00:07:33,537 --> 00:07:35,953
Cheap iron and steel pour in from abroad.

159
00:07:36,367 --> 00:07:42,634
By nineteen twenty four, the company needs close to two crore rupees, to pay its wages and the debts it owes.

160
00:07:43,053 --> 00:07:45,531
Where do you find that kind of money, fast?

161
00:07:45,930 --> 00:07:47,457
The banks want a guarantee.

162
00:07:47,686 --> 00:07:48,805
Something valuable.

163
00:07:49,706 --> 00:07:51,723
So we're back in that bank in Bombay.

164
00:07:52,019 --> 00:07:54,693
The diamond on the counter is called the Jubilee.

165
00:07:54,989 --> 00:08:00,503
It was found in South Africa in eighteen ninety five, and named for Queen Victoria's Diamond Jubilee.

166
00:08:00,844 --> 00:08:04,473
Around nineteen hundred, Dorabji bought it for his wife, Meherbai.

167
00:08:04,746 --> 00:08:07,508
She wore it at royal courts and grand occasions.

168
00:08:07,900 --> 00:08:13,738
Now Dorabji hands it over as the guarantee, with the rest of her jewellery, to the Imperial Bank of India.

169
00:08:14,049 --> 00:08:16,663
Today you know that bank as the State Bank of India.

170
00:08:17,122 --> 00:08:18,306
The loan comes through.

171
00:08:18,558 --> 00:08:20,016
The furnaces stay lit.

172
00:08:20,249 --> 00:08:21,673
The workers get paid.

173
00:08:22,660 --> 00:08:23,925
It was her diamond.

174
00:08:24,253 --> 00:08:29,319
And it went into a bank, so that families fourteen hundred kilometres away could eat.

175
00:08:29,808 --> 00:08:31,097
Did they ever get it back?

176
00:08:31,528 --> 00:08:32,061
Yes.

177
00:08:32,334 --> 00:08:36,133
We know because, eight years later, it shows up in Dorabji's will.

178
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:41,008
In nineteen thirty one, Meherbai dies of leukaemia, a cancer of the blood.

179
00:08:41,466 --> 00:08:43,613
The next year, Dorabji dies too.

180
00:08:43,973 --> 00:08:45,134
They have no children.

181
00:08:45,964 --> 00:08:48,469
And here is the turn in this whole story.

182
00:08:48,925 --> 00:08:51,489
He leaves everything to a charitable trust.

183
00:08:51,739 --> 00:08:53,254
His shares in Tata Sons.

184
00:08:53,369 --> 00:08:54,264
His property.

185
00:08:54,414 --> 00:08:58,756
And twenty one pieces of Meherbai's jewellery, the Jubilee among them.

186
00:08:59,059 --> 00:09:01,130
The Sir Dorabji Tata Trust.

187
00:09:01,641 --> 00:09:04,676
A few years later, the trust sells the jewels.

188
00:09:04,904 --> 00:09:08,565
And that money helps build a hospital for the disease that took her.

189
00:09:08,967 --> 00:09:14,014
The Tata Memorial Hospital, for cancer, opens in Bombay in nineteen forty one.

190
00:09:14,901 --> 00:09:17,061
So the diamond became a hospital.

191
00:09:17,418 --> 00:09:24,574
If you, or someone you love, has ever been treated at Tata Memorial, you've been inside what that diamond helped build.

192
00:09:24,975 --> 00:09:26,463
But the shares in Tata Sons?

193
00:09:26,807 --> 00:09:28,419
Those the trust keeps.

194
00:09:28,651 --> 00:09:31,288
And that means something no one had planned.

195
00:09:31,784 --> 00:09:34,957
A charity now owns a big piece of the empire.

196
00:09:35,246 --> 00:09:36,199
Keep that in mind.

197
00:09:36,311 --> 00:09:37,709
It's the key to the ending.

198
00:09:39,672 --> 00:09:41,796
Now the story needs a new captain.

199
00:09:41,929 --> 00:09:43,583
And this one flies.

200
00:09:43,832 --> 00:09:47,252
His full name is long, so everyone just calls him J.R.D.

201
00:09:47,654 --> 00:09:51,599
In nineteen twenty nine, he gets India's first pilot licence.

202
00:09:52,077 --> 00:09:54,654
The fifteenth of October, nineteen thirty two.

203
00:09:54,866 --> 00:09:55,486
Karachi.

204
00:09:55,700 --> 00:09:57,065
Six thirty in the morning.

205
00:09:57,509 --> 00:10:01,618
J.R.D. climbs into a tiny single engine plane called a Puss Moth.

206
00:10:01,896 --> 00:10:03,711
Behind him, bags of mail.

207
00:10:03,969 --> 00:10:04,866
No radio.

208
00:10:04,942 --> 00:10:07,821
No navigation aids, on the ground or in the air.

209
00:10:08,114 --> 00:10:09,958
Can you imagine flying like that?

210
00:10:10,417 --> 00:10:14,040
He stops in Ahmedabad, where the fuel is poured in from cans.

211
00:10:14,257 --> 00:10:18,270
Then he flies on, against the wind, all the way to Bombay.

212
00:10:18,601 --> 00:10:20,046
There is no proper airport.

213
00:10:20,174 --> 00:10:22,614
Just a mud flat at Juhu, by the sea.

214
00:10:23,116 --> 00:10:25,499
He lands at ten to two in the afternoon.

215
00:10:25,795 --> 00:10:28,376
That flight is the start of an airline.

216
00:10:28,642 --> 00:10:29,641
Tata Airlines.

217
00:10:29,733 --> 00:10:31,077
Later, Air India.

218
00:10:31,502 --> 00:10:34,645
For twenty years he builds it, plane by plane.

219
00:10:34,931 --> 00:10:38,564
But in nineteen fifty three, the government takes over the airlines.

220
00:10:39,094 --> 00:10:42,107
J.R.D. thinks it's a mistake, and he says so.

221
00:10:42,321 --> 00:10:46,037
So what does he do when they ask him to stay on and run Air India?

222
00:10:46,357 --> 00:10:47,251
He says yes.

223
00:10:47,510 --> 00:10:51,556
And he does it without a salary, for twenty five years.

224
00:10:51,878 --> 00:10:55,463
In these years, a company needs the government's permission to grow.

225
00:10:55,709 --> 00:10:57,587
What it makes.

226
00:10:57,893 --> 00:10:59,664
How much.

227
00:10:59,905 --> 00:11:01,435
So Tata grows slowly.

228
00:11:01,626 --> 00:11:05,328
But in nineteen sixty eight, almost quietly, it starts a small computer unit.

229
00:11:05,563 --> 00:11:08,785
Its first jobs are punched cards for its own companies.

230
00:11:09,031 --> 00:11:11,827
It's called Tata Consultancy Services.

231
00:11:12,145 --> 00:11:12,913
T.C.S.

232
00:11:13,231 --> 00:11:14,202
Remember that name.

233
00:11:14,693 --> 00:11:17,146
One day it will carry the whole empire.

234
00:11:17,548 --> 00:11:21,534
And in those years, J.R.D. gets a postcard he will never forget.

235
00:11:21,942 --> 00:11:24,076
April, nineteen seventy four.

236
00:11:24,201 --> 00:11:29,404
A young engineering student in Bangalore sees a job notice from a Tata company, Telco.

237
00:11:29,754 --> 00:11:31,366
At the bottom, one line.

238
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:33,744
Lady candidates need not apply.

239
00:11:34,190 --> 00:11:35,462
She is angry.

240
00:11:35,693 --> 00:11:37,263
So she writes a postcard.

241
00:11:37,525 --> 00:11:39,614
To the man at the top of the Tata group.

242
00:11:39,821 --> 00:11:43,925
How can a company like Telco treat people differently because of their gender?

243
00:11:44,289 --> 00:11:47,033
Less than ten days later, a telegram arrives.

244
00:11:47,250 --> 00:11:48,301
Come for an interview.

245
00:11:48,421 --> 00:11:49,136
In Pune.

246
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:50,671
She gets the job.

247
00:11:50,888 --> 00:11:54,313
She becomes the first woman to work on Telco's shop floor.

248
00:11:54,585 --> 00:11:55,653
You may know her name.

249
00:11:55,866 --> 00:11:56,834
Sudha Murty.

250
00:11:57,240 --> 00:11:59,904
But not every Tata story ends kindly.

251
00:12:00,345 --> 00:12:02,260
February, nineteen seventy eight.

252
00:12:02,526 --> 00:12:05,439
A new government removes J.R.D. from Air India.

253
00:12:05,724 --> 00:12:07,292
He is not even told directly.

254
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:09,929
He hears it from the man who is replacing him.

255
00:12:10,358 --> 00:12:12,973
That night, someone asks how he feels.

256
00:12:13,434 --> 00:12:18,321
He says, I feel as you would feel if your favourite child was taken away.

257
00:12:19,676 --> 00:12:21,029
Nineteen ninety one.

258
00:12:21,270 --> 00:12:25,851
India comes close to running out of foreign money, and the economy is thrown open.

259
00:12:26,077 --> 00:12:30,119
That same year, J.R.D. hands over to a quiet, private man.

260
00:12:30,453 --> 00:12:31,368
Ratan Tata.

261
00:12:31,669 --> 00:12:37,102
Ratan inherits a group full of powerful bosses who run their companies like their own kingdoms.

262
00:12:37,201 --> 00:12:39,501
So he brings in a retirement age.

263
00:12:39,679 --> 00:12:42,719
And one by one, the old bosses step aside.

264
00:12:42,917 --> 00:12:45,477
Then he makes his first big bet.

265
00:12:45,650 --> 00:12:48,481
A car designed in India, by Indians.

266
00:12:48,615 --> 00:12:51,670
The Indica, unveiled in nineteen ninety eight.

267
00:12:51,773 --> 00:12:54,725
About one lakh fifteen thousand people book it.

268
00:12:54,925 --> 00:12:56,641
Then the complaints start.

269
00:12:56,818 --> 00:12:57,481
Quality.

270
00:12:57,756 --> 00:12:58,276
Power.

271
00:12:58,504 --> 00:13:04,415
So in nineteen ninety nine, Ratan Tata and his team fly to Detroit, to the Ford Motor Company.

272
00:13:04,559 --> 00:13:05,975
To sell the car business.

273
00:13:06,192 --> 00:13:08,927
Tata veteran Pravin Kadle was in that room.

274
00:13:09,133 --> 00:13:13,933
According to him, the Ford people asked why Tata had started a car business at all.

275
00:13:14,074 --> 00:13:17,388
And buying it, they said, would be doing Tata a favour.

276
00:13:17,623 --> 00:13:18,969
The deal is off.

277
00:13:19,124 --> 00:13:20,838
They fly back the same evening.

278
00:13:21,042 --> 00:13:25,358
Kadle says Ratan Tata hardly spoke, the whole ninety minute flight.

279
00:13:26,937 --> 00:13:29,069
A long, quiet flight home.

280
00:13:30,291 --> 00:13:31,639
Hold on to that silence.

281
00:13:31,897 --> 00:13:33,122
So what does Tata do?

282
00:13:33,300 --> 00:13:34,343
It does not sell.

283
00:13:34,540 --> 00:13:35,759
It fixes the car.

284
00:13:35,926 --> 00:13:37,550
And it starts buying.

285
00:13:37,804 --> 00:13:41,486
In two thousand, Tata buys Tetley, the British tea company.

286
00:13:41,640 --> 00:13:44,753
An Indian company buying a famous British name.

287
00:13:44,932 --> 00:13:48,192
Then, in two thousand seven, the biggest bet of all.

288
00:13:48,361 --> 00:13:54,603
Tata Steel wins Corus, the company that included British Steel, for about twelve billion dollars.

289
00:13:55,115 --> 00:13:58,329
Remember Upcott, the man who would eat every rail?

290
00:13:58,665 --> 00:14:03,692
A hundred years later, an Indian steel company has bought what was once British Steel.

291
00:14:04,021 --> 00:14:07,495
But the year after that is the one that defines Ratan Tata.

292
00:14:07,723 --> 00:14:09,196
Everything happens in it.

293
00:14:09,475 --> 00:14:10,766
His proudest moment.

294
00:14:10,927 --> 00:14:12,224
His sweetest revenge.

295
00:14:12,443 --> 00:14:13,805
His hardest defeat.

296
00:14:14,606 --> 00:14:16,441
And his darkest night.

297
00:14:18,370 --> 00:14:19,167
January.

298
00:14:19,410 --> 00:14:19,976
Delhi.

299
00:14:20,283 --> 00:14:23,723
Ratan Tata drives a tiny car into the television lights.

300
00:14:23,934 --> 00:14:24,681
The Nano.

301
00:14:24,916 --> 00:14:26,857
A car for one lakh rupees.

302
00:14:27,192 --> 00:14:28,828
Costs have gone up, he says.

303
00:14:28,985 --> 00:14:30,829
But a promise is a promise.

304
00:14:31,116 --> 00:14:32,803
He said later what moved him.

305
00:14:33,047 --> 00:14:35,297
Indian families riding on scooters.

306
00:14:35,399 --> 00:14:37,598
Four or five people, on one scooter.

307
00:14:37,918 --> 00:14:40,088
He wanted to give that family a roof.

308
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:42,062
You remember that family, don't you?

309
00:14:42,300 --> 00:14:43,878
You've probably seen them yourself.

310
00:14:44,419 --> 00:14:45,094
March.

311
00:14:45,288 --> 00:14:47,971
Ford is selling two famous British brands.

312
00:14:48,074 --> 00:14:49,664
Jaguar and Land Rover.

313
00:14:49,937 --> 00:14:51,338
And who do you think buys them?

314
00:14:51,938 --> 00:14:52,480
Tata.

315
00:14:52,714 --> 00:14:54,988
About two point three billion dollars.

316
00:14:55,121 --> 00:15:00,809
And according to Pravin Kadle, Bill Ford told Ratan Tata, you are doing us a big favour.

317
00:15:01,144 --> 00:15:03,277
Ford has never confirmed either line.

318
00:15:03,460 --> 00:15:04,895
But the deal is real.

319
00:15:05,324 --> 00:15:06,046
October.

320
00:15:06,287 --> 00:15:06,950
Kolkata.

321
00:15:07,103 --> 00:15:14,290
The Nano factory at Singur, in West Bengal, has been surrounded by protests for months, over the farmland taken to build it.

322
00:15:14,433 --> 00:15:16,936
Ratan Tata announces he is pulling out.

323
00:15:17,069 --> 00:15:21,742
As he speaks, a one word text message arrives from the Chief Minister of Gujarat.

324
00:15:22,021 --> 00:15:22,654
Welcome.

325
00:15:22,875 --> 00:15:25,413
The factory moves to Sanand, in Gujarat.

326
00:15:25,643 --> 00:15:27,252
And then, November.

327
00:15:28,187 --> 00:15:31,036
The twenty sixth of November, two thousand eight.

328
00:15:31,330 --> 00:15:31,901
Night.

329
00:15:32,317 --> 00:15:34,158
Terrorists storm the Taj.

330
00:15:34,699 --> 00:15:36,114
Jamsetji's hotel.

331
00:15:36,388 --> 00:15:38,508
The one he opened in nineteen oh three.

332
00:15:38,855 --> 00:15:40,854
Inside, the staff could run.

333
00:15:41,076 --> 00:15:42,773
They know every back exit.

334
00:15:43,075 --> 00:15:45,731
But many of them stay, to get the guests out.

335
00:15:45,992 --> 00:15:50,731
A banquet manager, just twenty four, locks the doors and turns off the lights.

336
00:15:51,007 --> 00:15:54,906
She keeps more than sixty guests hidden and silent in the dark.

337
00:15:55,188 --> 00:15:58,608
In the kitchens, young chefs lead guests out through the back.

338
00:15:58,876 --> 00:16:00,985
A number of them are killed doing it.

339
00:16:01,244 --> 00:16:06,887
The general manager, Karambir Singh Kang, has his wife and two young sons inside the hotel.

340
00:16:07,209 --> 00:16:08,381
They die in the fire.

341
00:16:08,674 --> 00:16:13,290
And when Ratan Tata asks him to go and rest, he begs to stay and help.

342
00:16:14,547 --> 00:16:17,199
At least thirty one people die at the Taj.

343
00:16:17,484 --> 00:16:19,492
The fighting lasts three days.

344
00:16:20,756 --> 00:16:24,164
Twenty five days later, the Taj opens its doors again.

345
00:16:24,430 --> 00:16:27,699
The old palace wing takes almost two years to rebuild.

346
00:16:29,365 --> 00:16:31,612
Big bets come with big bills.

347
00:16:31,833 --> 00:16:35,255
A year after the Corus deal, the world economy crashes.

348
00:16:35,504 --> 00:16:37,526
Years of losses follow in Britain.

349
00:16:37,760 --> 00:16:43,252
And in twenty twenty four, the last blast furnaces at Port Talbot, in Wales, are shut down.

350
00:16:43,564 --> 00:16:44,765
Was Corus worth it?

351
00:16:45,023 --> 00:16:46,731
People still argue about that.

352
00:16:47,013 --> 00:16:47,774
And the Nano?

353
00:16:47,980 --> 00:16:51,285
People did not want to be seen in the cheapest car in the world.

354
00:16:51,515 --> 00:16:54,863
Tata itself admitted that calling it cheap was a mistake.

355
00:16:55,109 --> 00:16:57,105
Production ended in twenty eighteen.

356
00:16:57,345 --> 00:16:59,942
In twenty twelve, Ratan Tata retires.

357
00:17:00,079 --> 00:17:02,767
And four years later comes a boardroom war.

358
00:17:03,008 --> 00:17:06,525
The man who took over from him, Cyrus Mistry, is removed.

359
00:17:06,713 --> 00:17:12,247
The fight goes all the way to the Supreme Court, which sides with Tata Sons in twenty twenty one.

360
00:17:12,596 --> 00:17:15,052
The new chairman is N. Chandrasekaran.

361
00:17:15,304 --> 00:17:17,480
He joined T.C.S. as a young engineer.

362
00:17:17,869 --> 00:17:18,780
And T.C.S.?

363
00:17:18,889 --> 00:17:20,592
That little punched card unit?

364
00:17:20,779 --> 00:17:22,359
It's now the engine.

365
00:17:22,713 --> 00:17:29,700
Last year, about eighty seven percent of the profit share Tata Sons got from its companies came from T.C.S. alone.

366
00:17:29,996 --> 00:17:33,837
Then, in twenty twenty two, the favourite child comes home.

367
00:17:34,099 --> 00:17:38,493
Air India returns to Tata, sixty nine years after it was taken away.

368
00:17:39,068 --> 00:17:41,126
J.R.D. did not live to see it.

369
00:17:41,425 --> 00:17:44,270
But there's one more moment we have to stop for.

370
00:17:45,328 --> 00:17:47,051
June, twenty twenty five.

371
00:17:47,386 --> 00:17:52,832
Air India flight one seven one, bound for London, crashes just after take off from Ahmedabad.

372
00:17:53,167 --> 00:17:55,254
Two hundred and sixty people are killed.

373
00:17:55,510 --> 00:17:59,744
The final report is not out yet, and the cause has not been established.

374
00:17:59,970 --> 00:18:02,342
We remember every life that was lost.

375
00:18:02,590 --> 00:18:04,383
And the bets go on.

376
00:18:04,560 --> 00:18:06,962
Tata now assembles iPhones in India.

377
00:18:07,144 --> 00:18:11,149
It's building one of India's first big chip factories, in Dholera, Gujarat.

378
00:18:11,421 --> 00:18:14,990
When it will make chips at full scale is still an open question.

379
00:18:16,347 --> 00:18:16,912
So.

380
00:18:17,113 --> 00:18:21,236
Back to the bank in nineteen twenty four, and the question we started with.

381
00:18:21,531 --> 00:18:24,350
Why is no Tata on top of a rich list?

382
00:18:25,435 --> 00:18:28,447
Because the Tata family doesn't own Tata.

383
00:18:28,770 --> 00:18:34,146
About two thirds of Tata Sons, the company at the top, belongs to charitable trusts.

384
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:37,788
And the biggest of them is the Sir Dorabji Tata Trust.

385
00:18:38,028 --> 00:18:40,243
The trust of the man with the diamond.

386
00:18:40,429 --> 00:18:43,361
It holds about twenty eight percent of Tata Sons.

387
00:18:43,612 --> 00:18:45,049
And who owns the rest?

388
00:18:45,358 --> 00:18:52,160
Most of it belongs to the Shapoorji Pallonji group, owned by the Mistry family, and to Tata's own companies.

389
00:18:52,397 --> 00:18:57,939
So when you buy that salt, or that tea, a share of the profit flows up to those trusts.

390
00:18:58,074 --> 00:19:01,615
And out, into hospitals, research and scholarships.

391
00:19:01,829 --> 00:19:06,071
For almost a hundred years, that design held the empire together.

392
00:19:07,612 --> 00:19:11,511
Then, in October twenty twenty four, Ratan Tata died.

393
00:19:11,864 --> 00:19:15,740
His body lay at a hall in South Mumbai, and thousands came.

394
00:19:15,972 --> 00:19:16,862
Students.

395
00:19:16,869 --> 00:19:17,918
Ordinary people.

396
00:19:18,064 --> 00:19:19,981
Strangers who had never met him.

397
00:19:20,266 --> 00:19:22,132
He was given a state funeral.

398
00:19:22,449 --> 00:19:25,802
His half brother, Noel Tata, now leads the trusts.

399
00:19:25,953 --> 00:19:29,497
And in twenty twenty six, the cracks are out in the open.

400
00:19:29,742 --> 00:19:31,369
So what is the fight about?

401
00:19:31,590 --> 00:19:34,266
Who runs Tata, and who decides that.

402
00:19:34,545 --> 00:19:39,111
This September, the Tata Sons board voted to give Chandrasekaran another term.

403
00:19:39,364 --> 00:19:41,164
Noel Tata voted no.

404
00:19:41,408 --> 00:19:44,108
The trusts say that decision doesn't count.

405
00:19:44,341 --> 00:19:46,309
Tata Sons says it does.

406
00:19:46,819 --> 00:19:48,457
And there's one more problem.

407
00:19:48,742 --> 00:19:54,909
Tata Sons holds shares in so many companies that the R.B.I. treats it like a big finance company.

408
00:19:55,186 --> 00:19:58,527
And big finance companies must list on the stock market.

409
00:19:58,787 --> 00:20:00,683
Tata Sons asked to be let off.

410
00:20:00,912 --> 00:20:02,466
The R.B.I. said no.

411
00:20:02,805 --> 00:20:07,883
So Tata Sons may have to sell its shares to the public, for the very first time.

412
00:20:08,283 --> 00:20:11,307
As this film goes out, that fight is not over.

413
00:20:11,682 --> 00:20:12,394
Who wins?

414
00:20:12,615 --> 00:20:13,839
I honestly don't know.

415
00:20:14,061 --> 00:20:15,178
Nobody does yet.

416
00:20:15,603 --> 00:20:18,861
So in the end, this fight goes back to one choice.

417
00:20:19,184 --> 00:20:25,812
A man who had no children gave everything to a trust, so the money would go to charity, not to a family.

418
00:20:26,230 --> 00:20:29,566
Eight thousand Indians bet their savings on a steel plant.

419
00:20:29,844 --> 00:20:33,087
A husband and wife put up their diamond to keep it alive.

420
00:20:33,516 --> 00:20:37,325
And a hundred years later, the question is still the same one.

421
00:20:38,163 --> 00:20:40,950
Who should a company like this really belong to?

422
00:20:41,524 --> 00:20:42,387
What do you think?

423
00:20:42,778 --> 00:20:43,855
Tell me in the comments.

424
00:20:45,218 --> 00:20:47,187
This is Built on Bharat.

425
00:20:47,346 --> 00:20:50,689
The empires, and the habits, that built a nation.

426
00:20:50,879 --> 00:20:52,784
Next in Empires of India.

427
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:57,118
How did a group of farmers in a small Gujarat town build Amul?
